{"title":"1994 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 1994 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be two positive integers. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3958e984d2597b35da7975f4503cdcf965a777f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1ddf57a1507686a49e3d290b3542ccac565cd35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> different numbers from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5c95d2b1ee6b025d757ee65818daba20a1abe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2,\\ldots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> such that for any two indices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7ec5455ff7287eff220419970f446c62a141943a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i \\leq j \\leq m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e5e672a139e0b30661cf241c72ce8d487c58ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i + a_j \\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />, there exists an index <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db842618336b3fe437d3cbda6739ed306832966b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i + a_j = a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. Show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06990cbc064a33c31fe51653a1709b74d91f07c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1+a_2+...+a_m}{m} \\ge \\frac{n+1}{2}\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an isosceles triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the point on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is an arbitrary point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> different from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/200cef6bdf34aa21da8bdcbf721a3c6cb9feb45f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E, Q, F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> are distinct and collinear. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e523074f8e48f3c3e9e81ea84cfb36ddaa7b28a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c134d9eeaf3bf929d13b7bdd2545673458401e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QE = QF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/81232ecd8d9e4b5c0f24a00dabec238068f26de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> be the number of elements in the set\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/8/df892bcdef2499e61e89bfe7ad2690311b1ba52f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{k + 1, k + 2,\\dots, 2k\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" /> whose base 2 representation has precisely three <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s.\n</p>\n<ul><li>(a) Prove that, for each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, there exists at least one positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d85a5d05da0520a80b7b23b1c44b1c8216b21c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k) = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />.</li>\n<li>(b) Determine all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> for which there exists exactly one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d85a5d05da0520a80b7b23b1c44b1c8216b21c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k) = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />.</li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca10ffe3531cf1faf6222be7eac407c47bef878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd55252b72b418419d24dbee374a611e97265c0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {n^3 + 1}{mn - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"39\" /> is an integer.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of real numbers strictly greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />.  Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2d436be3e4977ddba9bdf67a9e8e6db508a44e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:S \\to S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> satisfying the two conditions:\n</p><p>1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e493e1c377107c62922ae655c978acffaed15dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x+f(y)+xf(y)) = y+f(x)+yf(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"320\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />;\n</p><p>2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed204d61675fd60a9f58e0ee455ae4e146b8dfb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(x)}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"40\" /> is strictly increasing on each of the intervals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/8/7e8c38956f2f71b857265a5b7b4168a070ac5577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1&lt;x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/b/28b30adeb3fd46044e00e82156ec3765c411dadd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Show that there exists a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of positive integers with the following property: For\nany infinite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of primes there exist two positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a758e08845ca74e10d1d9e3ab46113de7066c298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/1678b6a34ce0af2c238335b0e36e29d374fbc7d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\not\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> each of which is a product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> distinct elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17d88e2fdeef66df0e37def936f39b773567278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a> \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO\" title=\"1994 IMO\">1994 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1990\">IMO 1994 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO\" title=\"1994 IMO\">1994 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"externa